  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Paint Trees places copies of a prefab on the terrain. The terrain stores only each tree's position, size and colour, and draws them all together, so thousands stay cheap. Any prefab works, a rock as well. Height and width vary within a range, so no two copies match.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> You paint 100 trees. How many new objects appear in the Hierarchy?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Select Terrain 6 \u203A Paint Trees.\n2. Pick a tree; paint with Brush Size 10 and a low Tree Density.\n3. Hold Shift and paint to remove trees.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Unity Manual \u203A Terrain \u203A Trees \xB7 trees: LOLIPOP, CC BY 4.0 (Sketchfab)</color></size>"
