      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "A brush's shape is a greyscale image: white moves the ground fully, black not at all. With a heightmap as the brush, Stamp Terrain places a whole mountain, ridge or canyon in one click; Stamp Height sets how far it raises the ground. Any greyscale image can become a new brush.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> You double the Brush Size and stamp the same mountain again. Is it taller, wider, or both?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Select Terrain 3 \u203A Paint Terrain \u203A Stamp Terrain.\n2. In the brush list, pick Terrainstamp_Mountain_Brush; click once on the terrain.\n3. Double Brush Size and click beside it.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Terrain Tools manual \u203A Stamp Terrain \xB7 brushes: ambientCG, CC0 (asset library)</color></size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
