  m_text: "Large rocks are placed by hand as ordinary GameObjects, sunk into the ground so no gap shows under them. Small rocks in great numbers can go in Paint Trees. The same mesh, turned, scaled and half buried each time, stops looking like copies.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> Three copies of one rock: which one belongs to the ground, and why?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Select Rock A; move it down until no gap shows.\n2. Rotate it and scale it a little.\n3. Duplicate it (Ctrl+D) and place the copy with a different turn and size.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Asset library \u203A Rocks</color></size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
